n-names></name><name><surname>Nieves</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Formica</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>Randomised controlled study of effect of parathyroid hormone on vertebral-bone mass and fracture incidence among postmenopausal women on oestrogen with osteoporosis</article-title><source>Lancet</source><volume>350</volume><fpage>550</fpage><lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9284777</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b18-cia-1-367"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Looker</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name><name><surname>Wahner</surname><given-names>HW</given-names></name><name><surname>Dunn</surname><given-names>WL</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Updated data on proximal femur bone mineral levels of US adults</article-title><source>Osteoporosis Int</source><volume>8</volume><fpage>468</fpage><lpage>89</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b19-cia-1-367"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Marie</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Hott</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Modrowski</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1993</year><article-title>An uncoupling agent containing strontium prevents bone loss by depressing bone resorption and maintaining bone formation in estrogen-deficient rats</article-title><source>J Bone Miner Res</source><volume>8</volume><fpage>607</fpage><lpage>15</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8511988</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b20-cia-1-367"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Marshall</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name><name><surname>Lloyd</surname><given-names>EL</given-names></name><name><